{:itonami.blueprint/id "cloud-itonami-isic-3220"
 :itonami.blueprint/name "Manufacture of musical instruments"
 :itonami.blueprint/isic-rev5 "3220"
 :itonami.blueprint/domain :musical-instrument/manufacturing
 :itonami.blueprint/license "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
 :itonami.blueprint/social-impact [:worker-safety :materials-safety :consumer-protection]
 :itonami.blueprint/governor :musical-instrument-workshop-plant-operations-governor
 :itonami.blueprint/robotics true
 :itonami.blueprint/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :forms :dmn :bpmn :audit-ledger :cae]
 :itonami.blueprint/optional-technologies []
 :itonami.blueprint/status :public-oss
 :itonami.blueprint/maturity :implemented
 :itonami.blueprint/implemented-slice
 "InstrumentAdvisor ⊣ Musical Instrument Workshop Plant Operations
 Governor, langgraph-clj StateGraph, append-only audit ledger. A
 musical-instrument-workshop PLANT OPERATIONS COORDINATION actor for
 woodworking/metalworking/assembly/tonal-test lines producing finished
 stringed, wind, percussion, and keyboard instruments -- not direct
 crafting/assembly-line-equipment control authority. Four ops
 (`:log-production-batch` / `:schedule-maintenance` /
 `:flag-safety-concern` / `:coordinate-shipment`), all `:effect
 :propose` only. Twelve concrete governor checks elaborate this
 blueprint's four HARD invariants: propose-only effect, closed op
 allowlist, closed proposal-effect allowlist (no direct
 crafting/assembly-line-equipment control), permanent
 equipment-actuate block, independent workshop-equipment
 verification/registration before maintenance scheduling, independent
 batch verification/registration before shipment coordination,
 independent shipment-quantity recompute against the batch's own
 logged production quantity, double-schedule guard,
 instrument-family validation, pitch-accuracy plausibility
 validation, wood-moisture-content plausibility validation, and
 defect-rate plausibility validation. Safety-concern flagging
 (materials-safety wood-dust/finish-chemical hazard, equipment-safety
 concern) ALWAYS escalates to a human workshop supervisor;
 `:log-production-batch` is the only op eligible to auto-commit, and
 only at phase 3 when governor-clean."}
